Title: The Last Ferry
Credit: Sample film
Author: Continuo
Notes: Made for Continuo's sample project. Pictures: AI-generated with Krea 2 Turbo, shown as still clips, no generated video. Script and music: CC0.

EXT. HARBOUR - DUSK

= Ines waits for a ferry that no longer runs.

WIDE ON THE PIER

The sea is flat and orange. A small ferry sits at the end of the pier, lights off.

CLOSE ON INES

INES (30s) sits on her suitcase.

INES
It always left at seven.

ON THE FERRYMAN

The FERRYMAN (70s) coils a rope without looking up.

FERRYMAN
It left at seven for forty years.

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

= The lighthouse still turns for nobody.

WIDE ON THE LIGHTHOUSE

The beam sweeps the water. Ines climbs the rocks, suitcase in hand.

INES
Then I'll wait for the light.

INT. FERRY CABIN - NIGHT

= The ferryman starts the engine one last time.

INSERT THE CABIN LAMP

A single lamp. The ferryman turns a brass key. The engine coughs, then holds.

FERRYMAN
One more crossing. Don't tell anyone.

Ines smiles for the first time.

WIDE ON THE FERRY

The ferry pulls away from the pier, one light on.
